# Valentin — environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in what you need. `.env` is gitignored; this file is
# not, so it must never hold a real value — not even a truncated one.
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL. The server boots, the conversation works and
# `npm test` passes with this file empty: infrastructure values fall back to the
# dev defaults in src/server/config.ts, and an integration whose credentials are
# absent is simply not registered as a tool. That is the contract — Valentin
# says he cannot book a table yet, rather than trying and breaking.

# ── Core ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# Bedrock needs a profile with bedrock:InvokeModel — see CLAUDE.md. The default
# local identity does not have it and the agent returns an error fallback.
# AWS_PROFILE=dev-devops-agent
# BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0
# BEDROCK_GUARDRAIL_ID=
# BEDROCK_GUARDRAIL_VERSION=DRAFT
# PORT=3001

# ── Storage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `memory` (default) or `dynamodb`. Keyed on this, NOT on NODE_ENV — the
# deployed container runs NODE_ENV=production against a dev AWS account.
# STORAGE_BACKEND=memory
# DYNAMO_TABLE_NAME=ValentinTable-dev
# S3_PHOTO_BUCKET=valentin-photos-dev

# ── Auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supplied by infra/lib/compute-stack.ts. With COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID unset the
# server uses the dev-bypass verifier, which is what keeps tests and a bare
# `npm run dev:server` working. In production its absence is a boot failure.
# COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=
# COGNITO_SPA_CLIENT_ID=
# COGNITO_DEMO_CLIENT_ID=
# COGNITO_DOMAIN=
# DEMO_SECRET_ARN=

# ── Integrations ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hebcal needs nothing: it is a local calculation, so the Hebrew-date and
# Shabbat tools are always available. Ontopo needs nothing either — it mints an
# anonymous token per session.

# Amadeus Self-Service (https://developers.amadeus.com). The free sandbox is
# `test.api.amadeus.com`; the production host spends real money, so leave the
# default alone unless that is a deliberate decision.
# AMADEUS_CLIENT_ID=
# AMADEUS_CLIENT_SECRET=
# AMADEUS_HOST=test.api.amadeus.com

# Google Calendar + Gmail. ONE account for the whole deployment — this build has
# no per-user OAuth, so Valentin reads and writes as whoever owns this refresh
# token. Scopes: calendar.events, gmail.send.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# WhatsApp Cloud API, via the Graph endpoint for one phone number id.
#
# You do not need to register a number of your own to try this. Creating a WhatsApp
# app at developers.facebook.com gives you a sandbox test number straight away, and
# its phone number id and temporary token are exactly these two values. The test
# number can only message recipients you have verified there — add your own number
# as one. Leave both unset and the WhatsApp tools are never registered, so Valentin
# offers email instead of failing at a nudge.
#
# What the sandbox will not do is message anyone who is not on that verified list,
# and a permanent token plus Meta's review of each message template is the part
# measured in days. Messages Valentin initiates outside the 24-hour
# customer-service window need one of those pre-approved templates.
# WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
# WHATSAPP_TOKEN=
